# P27.3-log-rotation-fix -- real, standard logrotate config for
# alert_engine_supervised.log, the ONE file this project's own sustained
# dry run confirmed grows unbounded (31.8MB/165k lines with zero cap,
# confirmed via direct grep: no rotation logic exists anywhere in
# run_alert_engine_supervised.sh or alert_engine.py).
#
# copytruncate is REQUIRED, not a style choice: run_alert_engine_
# supervised.sh writes via a plain shell `>> "$LOG"` redirect held open
# for the ENTIRE lifetime of one supervised python3 invocation (hours to
# days in real deployment) -- a plain rename-based rotation would leave
# that already-open shell file descriptor writing forever into the
# renamed (now-hidden) old file, since bash never reopens a `>>` target
# on its own. copytruncate copies the current content out, then
# truncates the ORIGINAL file in place (same inode, same fd) -- the
# shell's already-open descriptor keeps writing to the same path
# seamlessly, no coordination with the running process needed at all.
#
# size 50M: real reasoning, not an arbitrary default -- the sustained
# dry run measured ~31.8MB of real growth over ~3 real hours under HEAVY
# fault-injection/alert-volume conditions (far above normal operation,
# where the documented PROBABLE/LOG-ONLY rate is ~22-25/hour). 50M sits
# with real margin above that heavy-load measurement (rotating roughly
# every ~5 real hours even under sustained heavy load) while staying
# large enough that one rotated file still holds a genuinely useful,
# multi-hour, correlatable block of real debugging context -- not so
# small that related events get fragmented across many tiny files.
#
# rotate 10: bounds total worst-case retained disk to ~500MB (50M x 10)
# before compression -- compress+delaycompress (below) shrinks that
# substantially in practice for this kind of repetitive text log, while
# still preserving real multi-day depth under normal (non-heavy-load)
# operation, matching the "beta tester running this for days" scenario
# this fix exists for.
/root/P20c_alerting/alert_engine_supervised.log {
    size 50M
    rotate 10
    copytruncate
    missingok
    notifempty
    compress
    delaycompress
}
